  "aiContextParagraph": "The 2026 Black Friday shopping period has seen extensive promotional activity from major retailers, with experts highlighting discounts on products ranging from electronics to skincare and fashion items. While large-scale commerce dominates the headlines with curated deal lists, there is a notable counter-trend among small businesses in the United Kingdom. Approximately two million small enterprises have reportedly decided against participating in the event this year. Business owners express concerns that deep discounting strategies may adversely impact their overall profitability and potentially diminish the perceived value of their brands. Furthermore, the broader discourse surrounding the shopping event includes regulatory scrutiny, as some Members of Parliament advocate for stricter bans on misleading sales practices before future Black Friday events. Experts continue to provide guidance on shopping strategies to assist consumers in identifying genuine value amidst the widespread retail activity.",
